# ─── Legal: unpublished patent materials (audit D-1) ────────────────────────
# D-1 / legal risk: docs/PATENT/ is currently TRACKED (git ls-files) yet this
# rule would silently ignore future patent edits. That is the worst state —
# either the material is public (then .gitignore gives false comfort) or it
# should be private (then git history still publishes it). DO NOT add new
# patent material until counsel decides filing strategy (see
# docs/PATENT/filing_checklist.md + CHANGELOG "Known remaining blockers").
#
# Suggested fix (requires counsel approval — do NOT run without it):
#   Option A — keep public and make ignoring explicit: leave this line
#              commented out so `git status` surfaces every PATENT edit.
#   Option B — make private: `git rm --cached -r docs/PATENT && git commit`
#              then uncomment the ignore below and force-push history rewrite
#              only if counsel approves (destroys public novelty anyway).
# PATENT removed from public tree per Engineering Elevation Blueprint §4.2 (2026-08-27)
# — re-enable ignoring to prevent accidental re-add.
docs/PATENT/

# ─── Internal audits — public hygiene (audit) ───────────────────────────────
# docs/assessments/ holds 6 internal audit dumps that are currently TRACKED
# and therefore public on GitHub. They are excluded from the published docs
# site via mkdocs `*Audit*` but the raw markdown is still world-readable.
# Hygiene fix (requires maintainer decision): move to a private repo / Drive
# or `git rm --cached -r docs/assessments` and add `docs/assessments/` below.
# Assessments moved to private archive per Blueprint §4.2 — keep ignored.
docs/assessments/

# ─── Local-only artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.zip
Q-Trust_v2.0.0_Senior_Engineer_Codebase_Audit.pdf
.ipynb_checkpoints/
Q-Trust*.pdf

# ─── GitHub kit delivery — profile repo is separate (humoge7502/humoge7502) ─
# The folder `profile-repo/` is a prepared copy of the profile kit for
# humoge7502/humoge7502. It is NOT part of the q-trust codebase and must not
# be committed to this repo. Create the profile repo from it via:
#   gh repo create humoge7502 --public   (or via GitHub UI: new repo named humoge7502)
#   cp -R profile-repo/* /path/to/humoge7502/ && cd /path/to/humoge7502 && git push
# Keep this ignore so `git status` stays clean while the kit remains locally
# available for delivery.
profile-repo/

# ─── qtrust_ai local artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Downloaded third-party dataset caches (real_datasets/ — hundreds of MB of
# cloned repos), fine-tuned transformer weights (crypto_codebert/model.safetensors
# — 300+ MB, exceeds the GitHub 100 MB file limit) and generated training
# reports are local-only. Rebuild via scripts/build_real_datasets.py and
# scripts/train_qtrust_all.py. Mirrors the .ruff.toml + pytest.ini excludes.
qtrust_ai/artifacts/
